      <activity id="3b204088-931f-5024-8de5-242fb6476fec" activityNameId="b1489552-b546-599e-b091-7fc19835257c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Disposal, carbon SPL, Al elec.lysis, 0% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Disposal, carbon SPL, Al elec.lysis, 0% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% spent pot liner, carbon fraction; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): upper heating value 22.2 MJ/kg; lower heating value 22.2 MJ/kg; H2O n.a.; O 49912; H n.a.; C 664640; S n.a.; N 13294; P 140.14; B n.a.; Cl 592.54; Br n.a.; F 79006; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As n.a.; Ba n.a.; Cd n.a.; Co n.a.; Cr n.a.; Cu n.a.; Hg n.a.; Mn 76.471; Mo n.a.; Ni n.a.; Pb n.a.; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn n.a.; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 13852; Fe n.a.; Ca 24707; Al 50831; K 4099.2; Mg n.a.; Na 98757; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%. Additional solidification with 0.4 kg of cement.;; UUID: 18e6fc6c-81e4-43c4-87c7-5e9a889a58a4
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. Expenditures for solidificalion with cement (user-specified option)
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_18e6fc6c-81e4-43c4-87c7-5e9a889a58a4.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
